  "PushingPixels-v0": {
    "description": "Stub entry for PushingPixels-v0 (BlockPush with RGB observations, single target). The PushingPixelsSimulation builds a (3*frame_stack, H, W) tensor at every step and feeds it straight to the conv encoder \u2014 the conv encoder handles its OWN preprocessing (uint8\u2192float, /255, bilinear resize to 180\u00d7240). The base-class ObservationNormalizer is constructed in __init__ but its `normalize(...)` method is never called in select_action. These dummy bounds exist solely to keep that __init__ from crashing.",
    "source": "Stub \u2014 never used at runtime; the conv encoder handles image preprocessing internally.",
    "observation_dim": 1,
    "flat_bounds": {
      "min": [
        0.0
      ],
      "max": [
        255.0
      ]
    }
  },
